(4968935, 723460, 84124, '<td valign="top">GREAT composition!  One of my favs so far, solid 7.  Really well done, very emotive, not sure if I want to think desolation or "the kids are all grown up"... probably the latter as everything is all overgrown.</td>', 'GREAT composition!  One of my favs so far, solid 7.  Really well done, very emotive, not sure if I want to think desolation or "the kids are all grown up"... probably the latter as everything is all overgrown.', '2008-09-22 18:50:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(4968945, 723572, 45475, '<td valign="top">Back to comment: Unsure how to critique this since the choices you made with post processing here is likely in line with your own personal artistic taste. Not a bad thing though!, and it IS interesting (in a clipart sort of way), just doesn''t particularly resonate with me.<br/> <br/>I''d encourage you to keep exploring new ways to present your vision, even if you receive less than favourable review. Still is a pleasure to come across something a little different once in a while :)</td>', 'Back to comment: Unsure how to critique this since the choices you made with post processing here is likely in line with your own personal artistic taste. Not a bad thing though!, and it IS interesting (in a clipart sort of way), just doesn''t particularly resonate with me. I''d encourage you to keep exploring new ways to present your vision, even if you receive less than favourable review. Still is a pleasure to come across something a little different once in a while :)', '2008-09-22 18:56:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(4968954, 723694, 45475, '<td valign="top">Back to comment: I also see XIX (19) in Roman numerals. Doesn''t mean anything of course, just what I saw before reading the title :)<br/> <br/>A pleasant image made a little more interesting because of the out of focus foreground. Slightly bothersome that the angle is skewed though. Taking the shot straight on would have levelled the lines and provided strength in the symmetry.</td>', 'Back to comment: I also see XIX (19) in Roman numerals. Doesn''t mean anything of course, just what I saw before reading the title :) A pleasant image made a little more interesting because of the out of focus foreground. Slightly bothersome that the angle is skewed though. Taking the shot straight on would have levelled the lines and provided strength in the symmetry.', '2008-09-22 19:05:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(4968964, 722733, 45475, '<td valign="top">Back to comment: Well seen! Great sharpness and contrast. The blown highlights are noticeable, but I can''t decide whether or it truly hurts this image.</td>', 'Back to comment: Well seen! Great sharpness and contrast. The blown highlights are noticeable, but I can''t decide whether or it truly hurts this image.', '2008-09-22 19:18:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(4968965, 723214, 98401, '<td valign="top">i like the fog.<br/>i think less exposed would make for a better mood here. i wish the bridge was level, though i do realize that would make the shoreline unlevel.. maybe just a different angle?<br/> <br/>i do see an M easily! cool shot</td>', 'i like the fog.i think less exposed would make for a better mood here. i wish the bridge was level, though i do realize that would make the shoreline unlevel.. maybe just a different angle? i do see an M easily! cool shot', '2008-09-22 19:22:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(4968970, 722565, 98401, '<td valign="top">the lense distortion is a little distracting to me.<br/>i also think it would be neat if you had the corner in thirds so we could see the left side as well, and a more shallow depth of field would also add to the subject. this shot is still appealing to me.<br/> <br/>i give it a 5... i think. im new here, and unsure about the voteing.</td>', 'the lense distortion is a little distracting to me.i also think it would be neat if you had the corner in thirds so we could see the left side as well, and a more shallow depth of field would also add to the subject. this shot is still appealing to me. i give it a 5... i think. im new here, and unsure about the voteing.', '2008-09-22 19:27:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(4968971, 723697, 45475, '<td valign="top">Back to comment: Amazing how it''s knotted up that way. Well spotted :) What I don''t like about this image is the background. Too many black voids with seemingly disembodied stuff floating around. Maybe a different angle or shallower dof to throw the bg completely oof would have made a stronger image?</td>', 'Back to comment: Amazing how it''s knotted up that way. Well spotted :) What I don''t like about this image is the background. Too many black voids with seemingly disembodied stuff floating around. Maybe a different angle or shallower dof to throw the bg completely oof would have made a stronger image?', '2008-09-22 19:27:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(4968973, 723736, 98401, '<td valign="top">i look at this and i think it would be cool to zoom out a little and left, wait for a car, close the app. down a little for a tripple A!!<br/> <br/>im more creative behind my computer rather than in the "field" though, so dont expect anything clever like that out of ME. :)</td>', 'i look at this and i think it would be cool to zoom out a little and left, wait for a car, close the app. down a little for a tripple A!! im more creative behind my computer rather than in the "field" though, so dont expect anything clever like that out of ME. :)', '2008-09-22 19:30:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(4968976, 722499, 98401, '<td valign="top">interesting photo.. looks a little blury up top. maybe a smaller aperture?<br/>i think that would help with the brightness too. i like the darker shots though.. cool anyhow</td>', 'interesting photo.. looks a little blury up top. maybe a smaller aperture?i think that would help with the brightness too. i like the darker shots though.. cool anyhow', '2008-09-22 19:32:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(4968980, 723451, 45475, '<td valign="top">Back to comment: Great idea, I like the set up. A few issues though - it lacks sharpness, there are spots (sensor dust or dirt on bg) that should have been cleaned up, and lastly, I think a lower angle would have been preferable so that the back edge of the table wasn''t slicing through the bottom of the pegs.</td>', 'Back to comment: Great idea, I like the set up. A few issues though - it lacks sharpness, there are spots (sensor dust or dirt on bg) that should have been cleaned up, and lastly, I think a lower angle would have been preferable so that the back edge of the table wasn''t slicing through the bottom of the pegs.', '2008-09-22 19:37:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(4969009, 723389, 45475, '<td valign="top">Back to comment: Such a wonderful shot of the bird. Not sure if it was your intention to have it out of focus this way. It''s not completely unappealing, however, would have been far better if it was imo.</td>', 'Back to comment: Such a wonderful shot of the bird. Not sure if it was your intention to have it out of focus this way. It''s not completely unappealing, however, would have been far better if it was imo.', '2008-09-22 20:06:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(4969012, 723456, 45475, '<td valign="top">Back to comment: The downward perspective skews the lines, making the image appear tilted. I do like the b&amp;w conversion though and the dof is great.</td>', 'Back to comment: The downward perspective skews the lines, making the image appear tilted. I do like the b&w conversion though and the dof is great.', '2008-09-22 20:08:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(4969020, 722168, 45475, '<td valign="top">Back to comment: Wonderful image. Nicely balanced composition and great depth. Love the way the light hits the building alone. I think you could have a bit of fun playing with the colour gradient in the sky too. The "V" is not the strongest aspect here but I think the moon works well as the "O". Nicely done.</td>', 'Back to comment: Wonderful image. Nicely balanced composition and great depth. Love the way the light hits the building alone. I think you could have a bit of fun playing with the colour gradient in the sky too. The "V" is not the strongest aspect here but I think the moon works well as the "O". Nicely done.', '2008-09-22 20:15:27.000000', NULL, 1),
